{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01275",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 5.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.93,
      "end_seconds": 10.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.41,
      "end_seconds": 17.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.84,
      "end_seconds": 25.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 27.9,
      "end_seconds": 32.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "doctor, it's a cough. That's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.52,
      "end_seconds": 41.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.23,
      "end_seconds": 44.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "probably one week. Yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.49,
      "end_seconds": 50.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.02,
      "end_seconds": 69.0,
      "duration_seconds": 16.98,
      "text": "I'd say a couple of times a week. Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. And there's a low fever as well, ten days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.08,
      "end_seconds": 77.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Is it it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.01,
      "end_seconds": 80.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "It's a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.89,
      "end_seconds": 84.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Have you had a sore throat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.98,
      "end_seconds": 101.63,
      "duration_seconds": 15.65,
      "text": "Yeah. Five days, I'd say. Actually, about sore throat, I'd give it a seven, out of ten. I had a tight chest before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.45,
      "end_seconds": 115.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "and what about shortness of breath, chest pain or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.45,
      "end_seconds": 118.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.23,
      "end_seconds": 123.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Alright, and what about leg swelling or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.9,
      "end_seconds": 132.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.23,
      "end_seconds": 137.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.83,
      "end_seconds": 139.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.19,
      "end_seconds": 143.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.5,
      "end_seconds": 147.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.0,
      "end_seconds": 159.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.66,
      "end_seconds": 175.39,
      "duration_seconds": 15.73,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure yes, asthma a neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it i just want to get back to normal, really mm, I've had heart failure, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.05,
      "end_seconds": 186.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure and heart failure, that matches what I have here. What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.17,
      "end_seconds": 202.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.4,
      "text": "I'm on lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.62,
      "end_seconds": 208.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Alright, since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.73,
      "end_seconds": 223.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "For two months. I take Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. Metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. I'm on paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.55,
      "end_seconds": 228.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.55,
      "end_seconds": 240.95,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I swim twice a week. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.72,
      "end_seconds": 244.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.45,
      "end_seconds": 251.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "yes, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.42,
      "end_seconds": 255.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.04,
      "end_seconds": 261.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "my grandfather had a stroke my mother had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.91,
      "end_seconds": 267.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.45,
      "end_seconds": 272.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Yes, plasters, it gives me a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.88,
      "end_seconds": 279.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.01,
      "end_seconds": 290.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.52,
      "end_seconds": 320.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 38.5 degrees, pulse 99, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, respiratory rate 17, pressure 118 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.81,
      "end_seconds": 326.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.4,
      "end_seconds": 330.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.47,
      "end_seconds": 345.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No crackles at the bases."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.05,
      "end_seconds": 349.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.1,
      "end_seconds": 364.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "There are a few scattered wheezes on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.59,
      "end_seconds": 376.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Putting it all together, it fits best with acute bronchitis. Another possibility is an asthma flare-up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.54,
      "end_seconds": 379.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.69,
      "end_seconds": 387.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like acute bronchitis, but I'd like to confirm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.98,
      "end_seconds": 433.99,
      "duration_seconds": 32.01,
      "text": "Let's book blood tests to look into cough. Let's get a chest X-ray, for cough. For this, azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for chest infection. Steam and warm fluids can ease the cough, and try to sleep with your head propped up. I'd like to see you again in ten days. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 434.61,
      "end_seconds": 438.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}